{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773163676,"nonce":"5KKJL4H8o4oLHBCOHAUF5NLxLEM=","title":"Issues tab: redesign from nested repo-tree to flat filtered list (auth-queue style)","message":"Current design uses repos as expandable headings with nested per-repo scroll areas (25vh each). This causes:\n1. Two levels of nested scrolling — hard to scroll-to-highlight reliably\n2. No branch filter mechanism yet (would require a third nesting level)\n3. Fragile scroll-to-highlight logic (3 failed attempts)\n\nProposed redesign (same pattern as auth queue):\n- Single flat list of issues\n- Combobox filter: level 1 = repo, level 2 = branch (only after repo selected)\n- Status filter (open/merged/closed) as toggle row above list\n- When navigating from another tab (monitor, auth queue, graph), pre-apply repo+branch filter so the issue is trivially visible — no scroll-to-highlight needed for the deep-link case\n- For manual selection within the flat list, no scroll issue (selected item is visible by definition)\n\nThis eliminates the nested scroll problem entirely, adds branch filtering naturally, and makes deep-link navigation simple (filter → item is at top of visible list).\n\nCodex+Gemini consultation requested before implementation.","files":null}]}